    <string name="map_teleport_help_title">Map Teleportation Guide</string>
    <string name="map_teleport_help_message">1. Stop the server before changing your spawn point.\n\n2. Tap “Map Teleportation,” then select All Areas, Calyx-Compatible Areas, or Exploration Areas.\n\n3. Select a World and destination Area. Review the Scene ID, Map Layer, spawn coordinates, and description, then tap “Teleport.”\n\n4. Return to the main screen and start the server, then log in to the game again. The new spawn point is applied when the server starts and will not move a character who is already in-game.\n\nThis feature only updates the scene section of persistent.json. Your previous settings are saved to persistent.json.bak before each change. The next change will replace that backup. To restore it, stop the server and restore the backup with a file manager.\n\nCalyx-Compatible Areas include the required Calyx combat data. In Exploration Areas, the Calyx is moved out of bounds to prevent accidental interaction and infinite loading screens. Use CN/EN in the top-right corner to switch the interface, Area names, and descriptions.</string>
